{% extends "base.html.j2" %}

{% block title %}Accessibility — {{ site.title }}{% endblock %}
{% block description %}How Brief APAC supports accessible reading across devices and assistive technologies.{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<section class="panel stack prose" aria-labelledby="accessibility-heading">
  <header class="stack">
    <h1 id="accessibility-heading" class="h1">Accessibility</h1>
    <p>
      Brief APAC is designed to be readable on phones, tablets, and desktops, and to work well with
      assistive technologies such as screen readers, screen magnifiers, and keyboard-only navigation.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section aria-labelledby="features-heading">
    <h2 id="features-heading" class="h2">What we support</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Responsive layout from small phone screens to large desktop displays</li>
      <li>Skip link to jump directly to main content</li>
      <li>Semantic HTML landmarks for header, navigation, main content, and footer</li>
      <li>Visible keyboard focus indicators on interactive elements</li>
      <li>Text resizing and readable line lengths on all screen sizes</li>
      <li>Reduced-motion support when your system requests it</li>
      <li>Dark mode support when your system prefers dark colour schemes</li>
      <li>Screen-reader text for external links and key actions</li>
      <li>Minimum touch target sizes for buttons and navigation links</li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://brailleinstitute.org/freefont" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="external-link">
          Atkinson Hyperlegible
          <span class="sr-only">(opens in new tab)</span>
        </a>
        — a typeface designed by the Braille Institute for low-vision and dyslexic readers, with distinct letterforms that reduce character confusion
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="compatibility-heading">
    <h2 id="compatibility-heading" class="h2">Assistive technology compatibility</h2>
    <p>
      Pages are tested for logical heading order, labelled navigation, and descriptive link text.
      Story lists use structured lists so screen readers can announce item counts and navigate by article.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="feedback-heading">
    <h2 id="feedback-heading" class="h2">Feedback</h2>
    <p>
      If you encounter a barrier while using this site, please tell us what page you were on,
      what assistive technology you were using, and what went wrong. Accessibility improvements
      are part of the MVP roadmap.
    </p>
  </section>
</section>
{% endblock %}
